[35.544903, "o", "pcfold/include/pcfold.h:16:int sf_index_objects(const char **obj_paths, int obj_count, const char *out_path);\r\npcfold/include/pcfold.h:18:int sf_render(const char *samples_path, const char *symmap_path, const char *out_path);\r\npcfold/src/main.c:10:    fprintf(stderr, \"       %s index --objects <o>... -o <symmap>\\n\", argv0);\r\npcfold/src/main.c:34:        if (argc >= 4 && strcmp(argv[2], \"--objects\") == 0) {\r\npcfold/src/main.c:55:            int rc = sf_index_objects(objs, obj_count, out);\r\npcfold/src/main.c:74:        return sf_render(argv[2], argv[3], out) == 0 ? 0 : 1;\r\npcfold/src/parity.c:83:        if (sscanf(line, \"%63s %63s\", key, val) == 2 && strcmp(key, \"FOLD_LATCH\") == 0) {\r\npcfold/src/index.c:88:int sf_index_objects(const char **obj_paths, int obj_count, const char *out_path)\r\npcfold/src/index.c:98:    int rc = write_symmap(out_path, \"objects\", \"object-merge\", NULL, syms, count);\r\npcfold/src/render.c:51:    const sf_sym_t *best = NULL;\r\npcfold/src/render.c:55:            if (!best || s->start > best->start) {\r\npcfold/src/render.c:56:                best = s;\r\npcfold/src/render.c:60:    if (!best) {\r\npcfold/src/render.c:63:            if (!best || s->start < best->start) {\r\npcfold/src/render.c:64:                best = s;\r\npcfold/src/render.c:68:    if (!best) {\r\npcfold/src/render.c:71:    strncpy(sym_out, best->name, 127);\r\npcfold/src/render.c:73:    *off_out = pc - best->start;\r\npcfold/src/render.c:77:int sf_render(const char *samples_path, const char *symmap_path, const char *out_path)\r\npcfold/src/render.c:110:        fprintf(out, \"    {\\\"pc\\\": \\\"0x%lx\\\", \\\"symbol\\\": \\\"%s\\\", \\\"offset\\\": %lu}\", pc, sym, off);\r\nsymmill/ops/pipeline.map:3:emitmap.gate\r\nsymmill/mk/foldlink.dep:3:\t$(PCFOLD) index --objects $(OBJS) -o $(SYMAP)\r\nsymmill/Makefile:14:.PHONY: emitmap clean hull\r\nsymmill/Makefile:18:emitmap: $(PROFILE)\r\nsymmill/contract.md:1:Fold pipeline bench notes. Source changes under `/app/symmill` and `/app/pcfold` are required before `emitmap` succeeds.\r\nsymmill/contract.md:3:`emitmap` must leave linked symmap + profile aligned with bench.samples PCs. Manual or hand-written symmap/profile files are insufficient; the normal `make -C /app/symmill emitmap` pipeline must regenerate them.\r\nsymmill/contract.md:5:Symmap header is `PCFOLD1` with `mode` set to `linked`, string `buildid`, an `origin pcfold-index-linked` line from `pcfold index --linked`, and `sym` rows. Hand-built symmaps lack that origin line. The symmap must contain at least 8 `sym` rows. Each `sym` row lists name, start address, and span size in hex. Span sizes must match `nm -n --defined-only` ordering on `/app/symmill/fold/runtime` (each symbol ends where the next text symbol begins; the last symbol uses a 64-byte span). Linked symmaps must not keep uniform `0x40` placeholder spans from object-index generation.\r\nsymmill/contract.md:7:Runtime `buildid` in the symmap must be at least 8 hex characters and match the `Build ID:` from `readelf -n /app/symmill/fold/runtime`. Bench anchor stamp `/app/benchframes/anchor/buildid.stamp` mirrors that value after a correct emitmap.\r\nsymmill/contract.md:9:`/app/pcfold/conf/latch.env` must keep `FOLD_LATCH on` so `/app/bin/pcfold check` enforces symmap identity. `/app/bin/pcfold check <runtime> <symmap>` must exit non-zero when the symmap buildid drifts from the runtime ELF and must exit zero for the on-disk pair after repair.\r\nsymmill/contract.md:11:The `/app/symmill/Makefile` `emitmap` target must run `$(PCFOLD) check $(TARGET) $(SYMAP)` after profile render.\r\nsymmill/contract.md:15:The verifier reruns `/opt/verifier/bin/pcfold-grade render` on held-out sample files without invoking `emitmap`.\r\nsymmill/contract.md:17:Profile `frames` are a JSON array of objects with string `pc`, string `symbol`, and integer `offset`.\r\n"]
